## PART A — FP (the priority)

### A1. THE TEST-ADMISSION GATE (the #1 miss: the pieces exist, the composition does not)
**Target:** fp_kill_protocol.md (new law above STEP 3) + fix-fp flow.
**Current state:** the fairness question, the reverse-direction audit, LAW N1, and mining all EXIST — but as separate sweeps run at separate times. There is NO single ritual at the moment a new killing test is born.
**Measured failure:** two self-inflicted over-pins shipped THROUGH a fully-run protocol and produced four consecutive 0-solve platform batches, 0/10 total (FIX #20; zips 55-58): one test gated a lifecycle corner stated NOWHERE in the prompt (it came from an FP variant-hunt finding, so it FELT like a closure); one pinned a corner via a clever disjunction that still rejected a third compliant reading. Both would have died at birth under a composed gate.
**Proposal (drop-in):** *No killing test is ADDED to the suite until its map row carries FOUR filled cells: (1) FORCING SENTENCE — the verbatim description sentence that demands exactly this, quoted; a stretch-trace (quantifier arguably covering the member) = STOP, use class N/fence instead; (2) F2P PROOF — the test fails standalone on the pristine base, or is explicitly a FOLD into a named F2P test; base-parity behaviors are ungateable, register silence instead; (3) UNPINNABILITY CHECK — could two correct implementations differ here? if plausibly yes, run the divergence test (A2) before gating; (4) MINING RESULT — the gate passes ≥1 real independent implementation (A3). A test lacking any cell is an over-pin waiting to be measured in a burned batch.*
**Why global:** every cell is repo-independent (prompt sentence, base repo, implementation plurality, mining).

### A2. THE UNPINNABILITY DETECTOR (new doctrine — the inverse reading of the differential)
**Target:** fp_kill_protocol.md STEP 3B leg 4 + FP_HANDBOOK.
**Current state:** the second-independent-reference differential treats EVERY divergence as "resolve which is right, add the killing test." For INVENTED features there is no external spec — some divergences are legitimately unresolvable.
**Measured:** three independent compliant implementations existed by the end (author reference + two commissioned); divergences measured between pairs — (i) mid-flight reads of just-created definitions (pre-transaction values vs undefined), (ii) notification coalescing for internally-driven transactions — each a case where BOTH sides satisfied the prose verbatim. We registered them as silences with the divergence as EXECUTED PROOF and our LOCAL adjudicator seat issued the explicit overturn rulings; the REAL panel's outcome (genuine pass, 'no fair discriminator') is consistent with those rulings, though it did not enumerate them.
**Proposal (drop-in):** *Differential divergences classify TWO ways: (a) one side violates a description sentence -> killing test + parity (existing rule); (b) BOTH sides satisfy the prose -> the behavior is UNPINNABLE: register the silence, cite the divergence as its executed defense, and NEVER gate it — a probe asserting either direction fails a compliant implementation and is overturned. The registered-silence entry gains a mandatory third field: the expected probe class it pre-overturns.*
**Why global:** derives from implementation plurality, which exists for every invented feature on every repo.

### A3. PRE-BATCH-1 MINING = A COMMISSIONED INDEPENDENT IMPLEMENTATION (fixes a real hole in the mining law)
**Target:** fp_kill_protocol.md "MINE THE CANDIDATE GATE" + FIELD_CARD validation law.
**Current state:** mining says "you already have N real implementations from the last batch" — **batch 1 has none**, so the only check that catches a 0-solve cliff is undefined exactly when the first (most expensive) batch is at stake.
**Measured:** commissioning an independent implementation from the DESCRIPTION ALONE (separate worktree, TASK.md only, never shown reference or tests) paid FIVE ways: solvability existence-proof before any batch, the differential oracle, the unpinnability detector (A2), silence-registry evidence, and architecture-class prediction of the eventual real solver. Cost: one agent-hour. The real solve's architecture matched the commissioned one's CLASS, not our reference's.
**Proposal:** *The independent implementation is commissioned AT CREATION (not submit time) and its full pass of the final gate set is the pre-batch-1 mining artifact. Post-batch, mining runs on real near-miss patches as today — and the near-miss that passes the post-lever gate set IS the Q3 solvability artifact (the strongest one this system can produce; we predicted the approved solve this way, FIX #20).* Commissioning protocol worth codifying: separate worktree + TASK.md = description verbatim + own scratch tests + regression run + report of interpretation choices (the choices ARE the unpinnability data).
**HONEST LIMIT (measured — do not over-trust this leg):** the commissioned implementation ALSO passed our two over-pinned tests (a commissioned agent, given unbounded care, implements corners that batch agents under real constraints do not) — so pre-batch mining proves solvability-IN-PRINCIPLE and catches true cliffs, but it did NOT predict the 0/10. Batch-solvability is protected by A1's forcing-sentence cell, not by mining alone. The two are complements, not substitutes.

### A4. THE WRONG-BUT-GREEN VARIANT MATRIX (new floor leg — probes and mutation both structurally miss it)
**Target:** fp_kill_protocol.md STEP 3B (new leg 6) + the 5x sim law.
**Current state:** the doc already admits mutation "cannot reach architectures the reference does not have" — but offers only the differential/mining as the independent source. Judge-c rehearsal = probe-hunting.
**Measured:** 10 probe-brief seats across two full local rounds missed a hole that the FIRST seat briefed to BUILD variants found in one pass (round 3; FIX #17: an alternative implementation shape passed all hidden tests while violating a stated sentence); a 16-variant matrix later re-confirmed every kill and adjudicated every survivor (FIX #19).
**Proposal (drop-in):** *Floor leg: build N plausible WRONG implementations as COPIES of the source tree (aliased test configs; never mutate the live tree), each embodying a distinct wrong ARCHITECTURE (lazy-where-eager, per-event-where-coalesced, registration-at-wrong-lifecycle-point, skip-one-module, order-swapped, guard-dropped). Run the FULL suite AND the base mode against each. Output a table: variant | hidden result | base result | killed-by test | or HOLE. Survivors adjudicate into: fenced / behaviorally-identical / no-reachable-divergence — anything else is a hole. Variant construction beats probe construction because it asks "what would a wrong solver BUILD" instead of "what would a judge ASSERT."*

### A5. THE TWO-MODE HARNESS IS PART OF THE FP SURFACE (new fact, absent everywhere)
**Target:** fp_kill_protocol.md + platform_spec stage 4.
**Measured:** the strongest attack our hostile seat constructed — a one-line slip inside the exact function solvers must edit, corrupting an untested aggregate — passed the ENTIRE hidden suite and died ONLY to the base/P2P slice (FIX #19). Conversely: base-mode exclusions carelessly widened would have reopened it.
**Proposal:** *(1) Every variant/mining run executes BOTH modes — a candidate green on hidden but red on base is caught by the platform, and the base slice must be CREDITED in FP defenses ("this class dies to P2P"). (2) Base-mode exclusions must never touch the modules under test, and each exclusion carries executed evidence (fails/flakes on the UNMODIFIED repo, N-of-M runs). (3) Local FP judges briefed to probe only the hidden suite will report UPHELD-looking holes the base slice already kills — the adjudicator seat must check both.*

### A6. THE PRE-WRITTEN OVERTURN TABLE (ship the defense, don't improvise it)
**Target:** fp_kill_protocol.md scope-out section + 04_create.
**Current state:** fences are prescribed; PRE-WRITING the defense table is not.
**Measured:** we shipped an overturn table (probe class -> verbatim fence/quantifier citation -> executed evidence) built by a local adjudicator seat (FIX #19); the REAL panel then found no fair discriminator — the outcome the table exists to produce, though the panel did not cite it clause-by-clause (honest attribution).
**Proposal:** *At creation, alongside the silence registry, write the OVERTURN TABLE: every plausible probe class on a fenced/silent behavior, the exact sentence that overturns it, and the executed evidence (divergence proof, base-parity proof, un-F2P-ability). It costs minutes, it is the FP panel rehearsed in advance, and on repeat repos it compounds.*

### A7. LOCAL PANEL SEAT MIX — BRIEFS OVER COUNT (amend the 5x sim law)
**Target:** pre_submit_gate 6B / fp_kill STEP 9.
**Current state:** "2 Sonnet + 2 Opus + 1 master, bar 4/5" — counts and model tiers, no brief diversity.
**Measured:** across three rounds, probe-brief judges PASSED artifacts that variant-matrix and dissent-hunter briefs FAILED (real findings each time); identical bytes, different briefs. A 4/5 bar where the 4 passes are probe-briefs outvoting a variant-brief FAIL would have shipped the hole.
**Proposal:** *Fix the BRIEFS, not just the count: (1) probe judge, (2) quantifier-exhaustion judge (clause-member matrix), (3) adjudicator (reference==prompt + overturn rehearsal + harness), (4) variant-matrix builder, (5) dissent-hunter (strongest single attack, argued both ways, self-adjudicated). Strongest tier on seats 4-5. A FAIL from seats 4 or 5 is never outvoted — it is closed, overturned-with-citation, or refuted-by-execution.*

### A8. FINDING DISPOSITIONS: CLOSE / OVERTURN / REFUTE (the third one is missing)
**Target:** fix-fp flow + fix_auto_review.
**Current state:** findings are closed (gate) or scoped (fence). A third disposition kept occurring: the finding is FACTUALLY WRONG.
**Measured:** a reviewer proved "dead code" with a 4432-test neutering experiment — refuted by a 10-line probe exercising the one path their experiment never drove (FIX #15); a harness "cannot execute" blocker was contradicted by ten graded runs (FIX #20; we still satisfied the CONCERN structurally — that pairing is the point).
**Proposal:** *Every finding gets one of THREE dispositions, each with an executed artifact: CLOSE (gate + parity), OVERTURN (fence citation + evidence), REFUTE (a counter-proof by execution — and where cheap, ALSO satisfy the underlying concern structurally so the disagreement never reaches a human). Refutations are pre-empted at creation by putting the executed defense of every "looks-dead / looks-redundant" design choice INTO the approach doc.*

