## PART C — SOLVABILITY x FP UNIFICATION (the user's core ask, stated as one law)

### C1. THE GENUINE-PASS STANDARD (what "solvability intact and genuine" operationally means)
**Target:** FIELD_CARD (solvability window section) + fp_kill.
**Measured chain:** gate only stated sentences (A1) + pin only implementation-invariant behaviors (A2) => FP-completeness IS the difficulty, and every remaining pass is genuine by construction. Evidence: the approved batch's only solve was upheld "genuine, high confidence, no fair discriminator" FIRST TRY, on a suite the adjudicator called "an unusually complete encoding of the prompt" — the same suite that, one lever-wave earlier with two unstated gates present, produced 0/10.
**Proposal (drop-in law):** *SOLVABILITY AND FP ARE THE SAME DISCIPLINE SEEN FROM TWO SIDES: a suite that gates EVERY stated sentence and ONLY stated sentences is simultaneously FP-complete (nothing promised is ungated) and maximally solvable for its difficulty class (nothing unstated blocks a correct solver). Deviations in EITHER direction show up as the OTHER side's failure: an unstated gate = a solvability cliff that LOOKS like difficulty; an ungated promise = an FP hole that LOOKS like solvability. The operational proof of the standard, both required: (1) N>=2 independent implementations pass everything (existence of genuine passes); (2) the executed floor + variant matrix run clean (non-existence of fake passes).*

### C2. ZIP-MATRIX RECOVERY, WITH PASSER COUNTS (sharpen the 0-solve ladder)
**Target:** prompt_fix_ai_runs / convergence law.
**Measured:** 0/10 -> 10% in ONE batch via: per-run failing-test matrix from the zips; the 8/10-failed test had 2 PASSERS (so not a cliff — but its behavior was UNSTATED = class F remove); the near-miss's 2-test blocker was stated-but-contested = class N narrow + class S symmetric assert removal; everything else = genuine walls left alone (FIX #20).
**Proposal:** *The recovery decision table keys on TWO columns per failing test: how many runs failed it AND whether a forcing sentence exists. {many fail, no sentence} = remove (F). {near-miss-only, contested sentence} = narrow + symmetric (N+S). {many fail, clear sentence, some pass} = calibrated wall, keep. {all fail, clear sentence, none pass} = cliff — disclose or restructure (D/R), never weaken (W).* This composes the existing F/N/S/W classes with the existing FDI passer-count correction into one operational table.

