### A5. Sampling is permitted where it silently produces false confidence `[SEVERITY: MEDIUM-HIGH]`

**Evidence + measurement (ledger row 85).** FP VALIDATION wave #4 mutated **10 of 30** atoms and found 1 hole. Wave #5 mutated the other 20 and found **a second**. A sampled sweep that reports "clean" is indistinguishable from a complete one in the log — which makes it *worse than not running it*, because it converts an unknown into a false green.

Related, same class (ledger row 83): **mutating all occurrences of a pattern at once hides which site is uncovered.** Three call sites, one ungated; a global replace killed the test and reported "gated". Isolate per site.

**FIX A5 — make it a hygiene rule in the floor, alongside the existing no-op-control rule:**

> **NO SAMPLING, NO GLOBAL REPLACE.** Mutate **all** atoms and **all** paths, or the sweep's verdict is void — report `N/M covered`, never a bare "clean". Mutate **one site at a time**; a pattern replaced at every occurrence hides which site was uncovered. Existing hygiene stands: no-op control MUST survive, positive control MUST die, assert the mutation applied (`count == 1`, `after != before`), rebuild in `finally`, **UNRESOLVED is never a pass**.

