### A6. Nothing protects the reference from the harness `[SEVERITY: MEDIUM — pure loss, no upside]`

**Evidence.** `FP_HANDBOOK` §1.7 requires "restore-verify byte-identical at the end, and assert it." Correct but insufficient: it protects the *completed* run. An **interrupted or concurrent** battery leaves a mutation applied in the reference and no assertion ever fires.

**Measured:** this corrupted my reference **twice**. Both times it was caught only by an explicit `cmp` against a snapshot — never by the battery's own hygiene. A corrupted reference is maximally expensive: every subsequent test result is meaningless and the failures look like real defects.

**FIX A6:**

> **REFERENCE INTEGRITY PREFLIGHT.** Before every battery run and before every regeneration: `cmp` the reference against the newest panel-confirmed snapshot and **abort on any difference**. Snapshot each wave (`reference_snapshots/solution.N.patch`). Never run two batteries concurrently — take a lock. **An interrupted battery is assumed to have corrupted the reference until `cmp` proves otherwise.**

