**Evidence, from the workflow's own text.** `/fix-fp` carries this admission: *"on the lopdf2 straight approval the sims cost 15+ agent-hours across three rounds and produced 0 of 9 real FP defects — all nine came from serially-executed mutants or from reading tests back against the prompt."* It then requires the gate anyway, pending two more projects of data.

**This project is one of those projects, and it is now reportable: `FOUND-ONLY-BY-SIM = 0`.** All five of my FP-decisive findings came from executed mutants, mining, or reading the panel verdict against the prompt. n=2 with 0 unique yield across ~20 agent-hours.

**FIX A7 — do not delete it; demote it and redirect the budget:**

> Demote the 5x sim from **mandatory** to **conditional**: required only when the executed floor cannot run (no prior batch to mine, or a repo where the battery cannot execute). Reallocate the freed budget to the executed floor's two quotas (A4), which is where **9/9 and 5/5** of the real defects have actually come from. Keep logging `FOUND-ONLY-BY-SIM`; restore the gate the moment it scores non-zero.

I flag this as the one recommendation the user should weigh personally: it *relaxes* a gate, and my standing instruction is that relaxation needs sign-off. The measurement supports it; the decision is yours.

