## ⛔ DEFECT D — "TRIPLE-CONFIRM" COUNTS REPETITIONS INSTEAD OF INSTRUMENTS

**WHAT THE DOC SAYS NOW.** *"run STEPS 1–8 in FULL at least **3 separate times** … Only when THREE independent
passes each come back FP-clean … If any pass finds a gap, fix it and RESET the counter."*

**WHAT WENT WRONG (measured).** My FP AUDIT #1 was three full adversarial passes of the protocol. It returned
FP-CLEAN. **The platform panel falsified it within hours.** Repeating a pass whose instruments are *mutation +
cheats I wrote myself* has near-zero marginal power, because pass 2 and pass 3 share pass 1's blind spot. Resetting
the counter makes it worse: it rewards the agent for producing three *identical* clean runs.

What actually found defects, across five rounds, was **structurally different instruments**:

| instrument | what it can find | its blind spot |
|---|---|---|
| mutation floor | behaviours the reference implements | architectures the reference does not have |
| cheat hunt | plausible-but-incomplete solutions | anything needing a real agent's design |
| independent second implementation | reference bugs, spec ambiguity | shared misreadings of the prose |
| real-patch mining | what actual agents get wrong | corners no agent happened to hit |
| cross-product cell probe log | interaction defects | single-rule defects |

The doc *already knows this in one place* — *"Forward and reverse are DIFFERENT audits with DIFFERENT blind
spots"* — but the confirm rule never generalises it.

**THE FIX.** Replace "3 clean passes" with: **"N INDEPENDENT INSTRUMENTS, each named with its blind spot and each
paired with a known-defective control it must catch. A repeat of the same instrument does not count as a second
confirmation."** Keep the reset rule but reset only the *instrument that fired*, not all of them.

**FIVE-BAR GATE.** Strip-the-nouns: passes. Fire-count **(re-verified): 3 of 11** — a clean-verdict audit later falsified (dolt, and two langium projects).
