## 3.2 Formatter subsystem map (`packages/langium/src/lsp/formatter.ts`)

The richest seam on this repo — three accepted/near-accepted submissions have come out of langium, one of
them here.

- `AbstractFormatter` walks the CST via `iterateCstFormatting`, collecting actions into a map keyed
  **`${offset}:${end}:${mode}`**, resolved by `existingPriority <= priority` (**later wins on a tie**).
  *Two actions on the same node+mode dedup; two actions from **different source nodes** landing on the
  same target do NOT.* That asymmetry is the single most productive FP seam in this file.
- A `FormattingMove` is only `{ characters, tabs, lines }` — there is no way to express a cross-line
  relationship. Any column/table/alignment concept therefore **requires a second pass**, which is what
  makes it a genuinely hard feature.
- `FormattingContext.indentation` is maintained *during* the walk, so you cannot short-circuit the walk
  without desynchronising indentation for everything after it.
- `avoidOverlappingEdits` tests `currentStart < lastEnd` — **false for zero-width edits**, so two
  zero-width inserts at one position both survive and stack. A real reference bug lived here.
- Edits are not inherently ordered by position; an append emitted at the appending node's offset can have
  a range *after* skipped comments. A **stable sort by (start, insertion index)** is required.
- `createHiddenTextEdits` **re-indents multi-line comment interiors** — which normalises `\r\n` to `\n`.
  This makes CRLF-in-produced-text effectively unreachable, but leaves **whitespace-only lines inside
  comments** intact, the one place they survive.
- CST helpers: `getNextNode(node, hidden = true)`, `getPreviousNode(node, hidden = true)`,
  `getInteriorNodes`. Pass `hidden = false` to skip comments.

